    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d801">

                <pb facs="0688" n="612" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg612"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/19756</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fort Sam Houston</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-10-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 25, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3456. Following received General Pershing dated October 24: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Villa in control of all towns from Bustillos west to Madera and all
                            territory as far north as Namiquipa and Santa Clara and probably east to
                            railroad. Carrancista detachment of 100 men at Cruces to-night.
                            Deserters say Villa still threatens to make attack on Americans as soon
                            as he gets more men and equipment.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Funston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
